🧠 Architecture Overview
 
- FastAPI (Cloud Run) = API Gateway / Work Console backend
- Cloud Tasks = Real durable background queue (replace BackgroundTasks)
- Firestore = Job database (no more in‑memory store)
- Cloud Logging = Structured logs
- Cloud Storage = Save generated knowledge artifacts
- Secret Manager = Load secrets (NOT hardcode tokens)
- IAM = Service Accounts permission chain
- AutoGenerateKnowledge.py / token_regen.py = Worker payload executors
 
💡 Why Cloud Tasks instead of BackgroundTasks: Cloud Run auto‑scales; BackgroundTasks dies if request ends — not suitable for real production
 
 
 
